      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)={e}^{2x+5},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=2x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2{e}^{u} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
